      "description": "Property. Model:'http://purl.allotrope.org/ontologies/property#AFX_0002684'. AFO 'quantified by': Relation of something that is quantified by some quantity value which expresses it relative to some other thing. [Allotrope] Flattened: in AFO the bearer is quantified by a quantity value (qudt:QuantityValue, typed with an AFO quantification facet class) that has a numeric value and a unit; here each item gives that class (quantity), numericValue, unit and optionally standardUncertainty. Typical uses: mass, volume, concentration, purity, pH of the sample."
